<title>RUSSIA: Russian helicopter designer dies.</title>
<headline>Russian helicopter designer dies.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aircraft designer, Mark Vainberg, who deisgne many Russian military and civil helicopters died on Monday in Moscow, an official for Mil design bureau said.</p>
<p>Vainberg, 49, has died of cardiac insufficiency, the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Vainberg designed widespread Mi-28, Mi-26K and Mi-34 helicopters.</p>
<p>Since 1992 he headed AO  Moskovsky Vertoletny Zavod (MVZ) which includes Mil design bureau.</p>
<p>He was a member of board of Russian, American and European helicopters associations, the MVZ official said. Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44-171-542-7706  Fax 5542-5017</p>
